# The Wi-Fi HAL reads its debug property on a build where that is deliberately
# not allowed.
#
#   avc: denied { read } for comm="wifi@1.0-servic"
#     name="u:object_r:persist_vendor_debug_wifi_prop:s0" dev="tmpfs"
#     scontext=u:r:hal_wifi_default:s0
#     tcontext=u:object_r:persist_vendor_debug_wifi_prop:s0 tclass=file
#
# `persist.vendor.debug.wifi.` (system/sepolicy/private/property_contexts:88) is
# granted to the Wi-Fi HAL by AOSP itself -- but only on a debuggable build:
#
#   system/sepolicy/public/hal_wifi.te
#     userdebug_or_eng(`get_prop(hal_wifi, persist_vendor_debug_wifi_prop)')
#
# Releases here are `user`, so the grant is compiled out and the HAL asks anyway.
# The denial IS the intended behaviour on this build type; granting it would
# undo a decision AOSP made on purpose, and the HAL works without it -- Wi-Fi,
# supplicant and hotspot are all up on build 71.
#
# Silenced rather than granted, and deliberately NOT wrapped in
# userdebug_or_eng: on a debuggable build the grant exists and there is nothing
# to silence, so the rule is harmless there and correct here.
dontaudit hal_wifi_default persist_vendor_debug_wifi_prop:file read;
